# Copy to .env.local and fill with your Supabase project values.
#   copy .env.local.example .env.local
#
# Dashboard: Project Settings → API

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_anon_public_key_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GLM server-only credentials (used by /api/analyze-closing-image)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Locally you can either:
#   (a) put these in .sec only (gitignored, recommended), OR
#   (b) uncomment them here in .env.local (gitignored).
#
# In production, set the SAME three values on Vercel → Project → Settings →
# Environment Variables. NEVER prefix them with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — they must stay
# server-side.
#
# GLM_API_KEY=your_glm_api_key_here
# GLM_BASE_URL=https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4
# GLM_MODEL=glm-5.3
# GLM_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# GLM_VISION_MODEL=glm-4.6v

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# M6 demo login credentials (demo v1 only — NOT secrets)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by the login gateway (app/lib/auth.ts). These are placeholder demo
# credentials for local testing; Supabase Auth replaces them in a later
# milestone. When unset, the defaults shown here apply. Because they are
# demo values (and appear in the client bundle), never put real secrets
# in NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables.
#
# Finance / auditor tab (المراجعة المالية):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LOGIN_FINANCE_USER=finance
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LOGIN_FINANCE_PASSWORD=finance
#
# IT / admin tab (مسؤول IT):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LOGIN_ADMIN_USER=admin
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LOGIN_ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin